As the tides change, the water level in a bay varies sinusoidally. At high tide today at 8 A.M., the water level was 15 feet; at low tide, 6 hours later at 2 P.M., it was 3 feet. How fast, in feet per hour, was the water level dropping at noon today?

A) 3
B) π\sqrt{3}/2
C) 3\sqrt{3}
D) π\sqrt{3}

Which one is right? Give the letter, then one or two sentences why.

When three standard dice are tossed, the numbers $a,b,c$ are obtained. Find the probability that $abc = 180$.

A) \frac{1}{30}
B) \frac{1}{72}
C) \frac{1}{71}
D) \frac{1}{70}

Which one is right? Give the letter, then one or two sentences why.
